  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">

      <p>CENTCOM struck M/T Downy, M/T Stark 1, and M/T Kylo on September 5 in the Gulf of Oman and northern Arabian Sea — three vessels operating on the Iranian oil-export route according to US DoD briefing materials (NPR, CNN, ABC News, September 5, 2026). The IRGC Aerospace Force launched ballistic missiles at USS Theodore Roosevelt and USS Curtis Wilbur on the same day; CENTCOM confirmed no hits. The exchange terminated the last active back-channel contact: Trump had ordered US envoys to halt contacts with Iranian counterparts on August 18, and the September 5 bilateral kinetic action removed the precondition for any near-term session in the September 17 window. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>Iran's President Pezeshkian stated at the SCO summit in Bishkek on September 1 that Iran would "immediately reciprocate if the US returns to its commitments under the June MOU" — a conditional offer that left the resolution criteria unmet before EOD September 6 (Al Jazeera, September 1). Foreign Minister Araghchi's August 19 declaration that "Iran rejects ceasefire and demands a complete end to the war" remained the last unconditional MFA position on file. No Oman or Qatar mediator readout of an Iranian acceptance was published before the September 6 horizon. The F2 ceasefire forecast horizon passed with YES criteria unmet, resolving RESOLVED-NO per ambiguity rule: conditional offers without US acceptance = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. → supports <span class="cite">F3</span> without move</p>

      <p>Iran's Foreign Ministry spokesperson Esmail Baghaei stated on September 7 that an Iran-Oman transit corridor agreement — covering a 7-nautical-mile-wide lane through the Strait of Hormuz, 60-day initial duration, no transit fees, IMO registration — was in "its final stages" (Bloomberg, September 7; Rigzone, September 7). An Al Jazeera report from August 26 had documented a "preliminary agreement" in late August. Brent crude settled at $96.15/barrel on September 7 after reversing an intraday decline attributed to the Baghaei statement. AIS data from Kpler/GlobalSecurity recorded 12 commercial transits on September 6; TankerMap/Windward reported a 7-day rolling average of approximately 21/day — a divergence exceeding the 30% ambiguity threshold in F4's resolution rule. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span>, <span class="cite">F6</span>, <span class="cite">F7</span>, <span class="cite">F8</span></p>

      <p>SNSC Secretary Mohsen Rezaei stated on September 7 that Iran would formally declare a restricted maritime area in the Strait of Hormuz "within days" (GlobalSecurity.org, September 7; IranWarLive, September 7). Tasnim News on September 7 quoted an unnamed IRGC naval commander as stating Iran had "completed preparations for comprehensive maritime defensive measures." IRGC naval units attacked three commercial vessels described as operating on an "unauthorized route" on September 5-6, per JMIC analysis carried by Reuters on September 7 — an action that also CONTRADICTED F4's primary indicator (sustained 72h halt in Iranian vessel-attack activity) and drove the net downward revision on F4. The dual Rezaei "within days" and Baghaei "final stages" statements originate from separate Iranian bureaucratic chains: SNSC vs MFA. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>A Maariv/Lazar Research poll published September 4 placed Yashar (Eisenkot) at 23 mandates and Likud (Netanyahu) at 20 mandates — a three-seat lead for the opposition bloc (israel2026.co.il; Jerusalem Post, September 4). An earlier Haaretz poll from August 26 recorded Likud at 19 and Yashar at 23. One Zman Yisrael/Tatika poll published in the same period showed a 22-22 tie. Likud's August primary concluded without a major leadership challenge, but the three available polls net to a Yashar lead averaging approximately 2-3 mandates against a Likud baseline that underperforms its Sep 3 projections. → moved <span class="cite">F5</span></p>

    </div>
  </div>

